    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which services does Significa offer?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We combine strategy, design and engineering to build digital products that are intuitive, user-centred, and built to last. That includes user research, product definition and proof of concept, UI/UX design, interface design, design systems, front-end and back-end development, infrastructure setup, conversion rate optimisation and growth strategy. In short, we help businesses define, build and improve digital products, especially during moments of transformation — like we did for mishmash and Hey Harper!"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you help improve an existing digital product?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Definitely. If you're falling short on conversions, your design feels outdated, or something just isn’t working as it should, we’ll help you figure out why and what to do about it. Since we don’t believe in one-size-fits-all fixes, everything we do will be tailor-made and shaped around your product and your goals."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What’s your creative process like?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our process is structured, curious, and collaborative. We ask open-ended questions, sketch ideas, and explore possibilities together. Closing our laptops and literally going back to the drawing board helps us pause, think, and work things through as a team. While inspiration has its place, great work comes from being present, putting in the effort, and staying open to new ideas."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer post-launch support?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Absolutely! Whether you need help with new features, bug fixes, or just someone to call when something feels off, we’ve got your back. We offer flexible retainers for continuous delivery or standalone support scopes, depending on what makes sense for your digital product and your team."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does a typical project team look like?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We build each team around your product’s needs. Most projects include full-time Designers and/or Engineers who work either for the entire project duration or until a specific milestone is completed. Depending on scope, they’re supported by partially allocated roles that bring strategic oversight and operational support. The Creative Director oversees UI/UX design, ensures brand consistency, and leads feedback loops for continuous improvement. The Tech Lead plans technical architecture and coordinates cross-team development to ensure seamless API integrations and system interoperability. The Project and/or Product Manager connects business, design, and development, driving the product vision and roadmap, prioritising features for impact and user value, and leading agile processes through to launch. The Delivery Manager ensures process efficiency and exceptional quality across all deliverables. C-level support is available when relevant and aligned with your project’s scope and budget. Want to know what happens next? Here’s how we get a project started."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What’s with all the design awards?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We’re super proud of them, but they’re more than shiny trophies. Design is at the heart of everything we do at Significa. It shapes how we connect with people, solve problems, and make an impact. Each design awardcelebrates this mindset, the effort behind every project, and connects us to a global community that values creativity, curiosity, and innovation. More than anything, it’s a reminder to keep pushing boundaries and delivering work we believe in."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

